{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs","id":359471,"title":"Should I kill PCs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-04T13:20:03-08:00","id":359471,"title":"Should I kill PCs?","content":"My chronicle have a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359371-wicked-bale-hounds-vs-uber-rahu-and-a-rest-of-pack\">near-final fight with Bale Hounds</a>. Character have almost all Health boxes filled with Aggravated wounds, Essence depleted, enemies still standing. And player still do not want to retreat from the fight.<br /> <br /> It is probably the suicide fight, PCs will probably not win. On general, in RPG, I make PCs very tired, used almost all resources, having extra scars or even lost a limb. But PCs, in my games, <b>live</b>. At least till player say he want his character to die.<br /> <br /> But the <b>Werewolf</b> is very violent game about warriors fighting impossible battles. Some of PCs should die, from time to time, I reason from the sound of writing in corebook. And this fight looks like it could be last for PCs.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's a bit pre-mature ending to chronicle - I still want PCs to explore a Wound I put as end game stuff, and go down in to Hell from it. There, as I planned, some character can sacrifice themsvles to seal the damn thing and maybe one or two PCs could return to normal world.<br /> <br /> I once saved the one PC on today's game session - he would be dead if I'm not &quot;miscalculated somethings&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />But saving players every time they made half-stupid choice is also bad, in my POV. If they fight noble, but unwinnable combat, should not they lose?<br /> <br /> But on the third hand - each death should be meaningful, yes? So maybe PC will die at the hand of their enemies, but at least rest of the pack can fulfill the mission?<br /> <br /> I'm very torn on what to do in game... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:28:26-08:00","id":359491,"title":"","content":"As a player I would say: Let them die.<br /> <br /> As you mention, they are in bad shape, their resource depleted and they wish to move on in a near suicidal situation...Give them what they deserve.<br /> <br /> I have no problem when a GM or ST give players the odd chances when a bad roll would otherwise kill them or make a good plan fail on a fluke. But rewarding them by saving their ass when they make bad/stupid decisions just encourage them to continue down that road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":".  typo 01-04-2015, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:35:04-08:00","id":359496,"title":"","content":"Ok let me ask a few questions. If you do kill some characters, what can you do to keep the players of those dead characters entertained? Are there allies they could take control of? You say you normally don't kill off characters? Have your currents players gamed with you before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>1","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27-ulfsarkar","name":"Ulfsarkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T13:38:08-08:00","id":359500,"title":"","content":"My answer to having player characters die is that you should kill them if the natural sequence of events leads to it being a reasonable conclusion. It is unfair to the players to spring a sudden trap on them with no warning and they all die with no way of being able to avoid it, but it sounds like your game has been building to this moment and that player death would be a reasonable outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T14:13:51-08:00","id":359523,"title":"","content":"It depends on the situation. Not everyone's going to be out to kill entire groups of people, they might just be fine getting away or driving the players off.<br /> <br /> But from what you've said about the situation, it sounds like the players have chosen to make a last stand against overwhelming odds, and most of the group is already dead. In which case if the numbers look like they're leaning towards it there's only a few reasons you should abstain. Of course, as dark as it may seem, there's no reason good things can't come from death, particularly such a thematically powerful one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T14:20:47-08:00","id":359527,"title":"","content":"They should die.<br /> <br /> If I were one of the players, I'd feel like I was cheated of a glorious death for my character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T15:37:39-08:00","id":359623,"title":"","content":"My general view is that GMs ought to do all they can to keep up the Threat of Death (since this keeps the game tense), while pulling the trigger as little as they can possibly get away with (since that ends any dramatic or story arc that the character had, and ends all the investment in them). So I'm usually in your camp regarding PC death.<br /> <br /> That said, if the players are knowingly going for a Glorious Last Stand, well then, I'd feel cheated if I'd opted for a heroic sacrifice of my character and then some Deus Ex Machina came along. It can actually be kind of liberating, when all involved know that survival is not an option, since then you can make the deaths as memorable as possible.<br /> <br /> So my advice here is to be sure that the players are aware that this is going to lead to their (likely) deaths -- just ask them in OOC &quot;you guys know you're probably all going to die now, right?&quot; -- and if they still want to forge ahead, then fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T16:01:47-08:00","id":359637,"title":"","content":"If you have already given them an out (i.e. the ability to retreat), then that's really all you can do. If the situation says they're dead, they're dead IMO.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you do make death a consequence, you might get a situation where only one character dies and the others realise 'oh... run away! run away! bravely run away!' So just plan for that, too. Plan a way for the game to continue and the players to continue playing, but don't hold back when it comes to killing their characters if the time has come...<br /> <br /> Unless they're all really anti-character death..?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T20:11:36-08:00","id":359834,"title":"","content":"I'd have to agree with most people, particularly NeoTiamat. Combat has no tension if there's no chance it could end badly: of course, badly doesn't always mean fatal. But in this context, seems pretty obvious that it does. I'd be very clear with the players that the fight they're choosing is near-certainly going to kill them, and if they choose to keep going, then let it unfold (rolling openly if you're concerned they could get angry).<br /> <br /> Of course, there's a potential deeper problem. I don't know your group, so I can't comment on their specific case, but if a group is throwing themselves into a suicidal option, it <i>might</i> indicate that they're bored or otherwise not enjoying the game and want it to end, even if so with a TPK. In which case, the outcome really isn't important, but rather the underlying situation. Maybe your ST-ing isn't to a style they enjoy, or maybe there's just something about this game that isn't grabbing them. Like I said, I don't know the group, so I may be entirely wrong here. Just seems a potential aspect.<br /> <br /> As always in RPing, the key is trust and communication between players and ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T00:07:13-08:00","id":359947,"title":"","content":"<b>General notice:</b> One of players could not end with us the story, so he wanted to kill his character in meaningful way. He is outside of combat circle, with rest of PCs been encircled by Bale Hounds and corrupted spirits. We have idea that his Cathalith from Hunters in Darkness will rush in to circle of enemies to break encirclement, and lend other PCs way out. He will be killed by his enemies in blaze of glory in the protection of Locus, but will find other Forsaken way out.<br /> <br /> The question is changed then \u2013 <b>if Rahu player insist on fighting after his comrade has sacrificed his life to let them out, should he be killed?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=359523#post359523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the situation. Not everyone's going to be out to kill entire groups of people, they might just be fine getting away or driving the players off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly this kind of GM. I do not killed random PC by... I do not know, 10 years? I just do not like to kill PCs as I know the players putted all the time and energy in creating and developing character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=359523#post359523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But from what you've said about the situation, it sounds like the players have chosen to make a last stand against overwhelming odds, and most of the group is already dead. In which case if the numbers look like they're leaning towards it there's only a few reasons you should abstain. Of course, as dark as it may seem, there's no reason good things can't come from death, particularly such a thematically powerful one.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRest of characters is <b>on</b> <b>brink</b> of death. They could make something, but it would probably would be their last action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=359623#post359623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general view is that GMs ought to do all they can to keep up the Threat of Death (since this keeps the game tense), while pulling the trigger as little as they can possibly get away with (since that ends any dramatic or story arc that the character had, and ends all the investment in them). So I'm usually in your camp regarding PC death.<br /> <br /> That said, if the players are knowingly going for a Glorious Last Stand, well then, I'd feel cheated if I'd opted for a heroic sacrifice of my character and then some Deus Ex Machina came along. It can actually be kind of liberating, when all involved know that survival is not an option, since then you can make the deaths as memorable as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was assuming it was the decision of player to end his life in blaze of glory, but when he was hitted with deadly attack it was \u201cWhat? You killed me now.\u201d Then I undue my last calculations to save him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=359623#post359623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my advice here is to be sure that the players are aware that this is going to lead to their (likely) deaths -- just ask them in OOC &quot;you guys know you're probably all going to die now, right?&quot; -- and if they still want to forge ahead, then fair enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will mark to the player that his character will die if he insist on fighting on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=359637#post359637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they're all really anti-character death..?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know \u2013 they are my buddies from our RPG club, but it\u2019s first game we play together. But Rahu player looks like he want to be both invincible and rolling to fight every time. What is weird, as player is normally an cVampire Storyteller, rather experienced one, so he should know characters should die in RPGs, sometimes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=359834#post359834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Of course, there's a potential deeper problem. I don't know your group, so I can't comment on their specific case, but if a group is throwing themselves into a suicidal option, it <i>might</i> indicate that they're bored or otherwise not enjoying the game and want it to end, even if so with a TPK. In which case, the outcome really isn't important, but rather the underlying situation. Maybe your ST-ing isn't to a style they enjoy, or maybe there's just something about this game that isn't grabbing them. Like I said, I don't know the group, so I may be entirely wrong here. Just seems a potential aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not think it\u2019s the way, as only Rahu player is rolling in this for combat, rest is rather looking for tactical solutions, with ambushes and reconnaissance. Problem is that he is Alpha of pack, so even if other players do not agree with him, he just throws threats and himself in danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T02:47:09-08:00","id":360054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem is that he is Alpha of pack, so even if other players do not agree with him, he just throws threats and himself in danger. </div> </div> </div>He sounds a pretty bad alpha. Frankly the others should just leave him to his stupidity... and the Bale Hounds. You could pass them notes saying as such.<br /> <br /> I mean, being easy on killing players is fine, as long as players don't start thinking they can just do whatever and nothing bad's ever going to happen as a result. You already handed them a way out and they didn't take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T03:37:37-08:00","id":360091,"title":"","content":"I normally get more and more clever the closer my characters get to dying. If they go charging at the proverbial tsunami without much of a plan, let the game end in tragedy. It was the character's choice in the end. Let them know if they're taking the path of the doomed ronin, tho.<br /> <br /> If the odds are stacked against them? give them 1 chance. The proverbial linchpin on their enemies plot, the glowing, shimmering light of hope of managing to beat the odds, and destroy the Death Star.<br /> <br /> It would cheapen all of my gaming experience if the ST pulled some Deus Ex Machina to save my character's ass in the last second. It's anti-climatic as hell. Look at how Dark Knight Rises went.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 01-05-2015, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T04:05:33-08:00","id":360100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=360091#post360091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would cheapen all of my gaming experience if the ST pulled some Deus Ex Machina to save my character's ass in the last second. It's anti-climatic as hell. Look at how Dark Knight Rises went.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that's hardly fair.<br /> <br /> The Dark Knight Rises failed in many, many other ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T05:19:05-08:00","id":360130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=360054#post360054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He sounds a pretty bad alpha. Frankly the others should just leave him to his stupidity... and the Bale Hounds. You could pass them notes saying as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, he does seem like a bad Alpha who's out there for his personal glory and he doesn't care who dies along the way. <br /> <br /> They should feel free to tell him : &quot;Look, we are in a bad shape and cannot continue onward, we need to retreat and recover, then come back with a better plan.&quot; If the alpha wants to continue on, they should leave him to his own devise and chose a new alpha","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:13:53-08:00","id":363164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=360130#post360130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, he does seem like a bad Alpha who's out there for his personal glory and he doesn't care who dies along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, he's a Glory Hound? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T07:36:57-08:00","id":363481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=363164#post363164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, he's a Glory Hound? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>(Getting a rolled up newspaper) Bad Allan53, bad boy (hit him on the nose). No bad puns. They are not allowed -even if accurate.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T09:02:37-08:00","id":363555,"title":"","content":"Actions have consequences, stupid actions have severe consequences. If an unusually bad die roll is causing an issue with your story I'd say ignore it or downgrade the impact, If the player/pc is acting unusually stupidly give them a heads up that bad things will happen if they continue on their path, and ask them if this behavior is consistent with how they've been playing the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T20:55:43-08:00","id":365065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/359471-should-i-kill-pcs?p=363555#post363555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actions have consequences, stupid actions have severe consequences. If an unusually bad die roll is causing an issue with your story I'd say ignore it or downgrade the impact, If the player/pc is acting unusually stupidly give them a heads up that bad things will happen if they continue on their path, and ask them if this behavior is consistent with how they've been playing the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the heart of it really, actions have consequences and part of the job as a storyteller is to act upon them albeit with fair warning if the characters are acting grossly out of character. Still, if you gave warnings that character death may result and they are continuing on this path, then you must do what needs to be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}